{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Q-functions of the ABJM HW states and LR symmetry\n\n**Question (Paul).** In 2603 LR symmetry is Q₁ = Q₁₂₃ (equivalently Q_j ∝ Q^{5−j} up to Q-system symmetries). Build the Q-functions of all saved ABJM states (`data/abjm-hw-states.wxf`, L = 2, 3, 4 pairs, untwisted, ABJM point θ_A = θ_F + 2h) and test this.\n\n**Method.**\n1. Eigenvalue polynomials τ̄_a(u), a = 1, 2, 3 (degree 2L) by interpolation of the one-pass transfer matrices on each state; full τ_a = ∏_s g_s · τ̄_a (τ₁ = τ̄₁), τ₄ = qdet T.\n2. Baxter equation for single-index Q's (Talalaev form Σ_a (−1)^a τ_a(u) e^{−ah∂} with columns u, u−h, …), in polynomial gauge: Σ_{a=0}^{4} (−1)^a τ_a(u) Q(u + h − ah) ∏_{b=a}^{3} d(u − bh) = 0, with d a vacuum eigenvalue of a diagonal T_aa. (For su(2) this reproduces a(u)Q(u−h) − τ(u)Q(u) + d(u)Q(u+h) = 0 with d = T₂₂ on the vacuum; for su(4) the choice of d is tested on the vacuum.)\n3. Polynomial solutions Q₁, Q₂, Q₃, Q₄ ordered by degree; Q₁₂ = Cas(Q₁, Q₂), Q₁₂₃ = Cas(Q₁, Q₂, Q₃) (Casoratians with shifts 0, −h, − 2h). Degree checks against the magnon numbers K₁, K₂, K₃ from the Dynkin label: K₂ = L − (p+r)/2 − q, K₁ = (L − p + K₂)/2, K₃ = (L − r + K₂)/2.\n4. LR test: Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(u + c)? Compare with the transfer-matrix LR defect δ_LR and check that 𝒫 maps Q₁ ↔ Q₁₂₃ of the partner.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[ee, rho, lax1, lax2, lax3, wedgeC, Dw, wedgeOp, applySite, typesOf, transferV, thAB, t1b, t2b, t3b];\nnn = 4; hh = 1/2; thA = 2 hh; thF = 0;\nee[i_, j_] := SparseArray[{{i, j}} -> 1, {nn, nn}];\nrho[\"A\"][i_, j_] := ee[i, j]; rho[\"F\"][i_, j_] := -ee[j, i];\nid4 = IdentityMatrix[nn, SparseArray];\nlax1[ty_][v_, t_][i_, j_] := (v - t) KroneckerDelta[i, j] id4 + hh rho[ty][i, j];\nlax3[\"A\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t + hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 - hh ee[l, k];\nlax3[\"F\"][v_, t_][k_, l_] := (v - t - 3 hh) KroneckerDelta[k, l] id4 + hh ee[k, l];\nsubs2 = Subsets[Range[nn], {2}];\nwedgeC[k_, m_, Ir_] := Which[{k, m} == Ir, 1, {m, k} == Ir, -1, True, 0];\nDw[X_] := Table[Sum[X[[k, Jc[[1]]]] wedgeC[k, Jc[[2]], Ir] + X[[k, Jc[[2]]]] wedgeC[Jc[[1]], k, Ir], {k, nn}], {Ir, subs2}, {Jc, subs2}];\nDwE = Table[Dw[Normal[ee[a, b]]], {a, nn}, {b, nn}];\nwedgeOp[ty_][iI_, iJ_] := wedgeOp[ty][iI, iJ] = Sum[DwE[[a, b, iI, iJ]] rho[ty][a, b], {a, nn}, {b, nn}];\nlax2[ty_][v_, t_][iI_, iJ_] := (v - t - If[ty == \"F\", hh, 0]) KroneckerDelta[iI, iJ] id4 + hh wedgeOp[ty][iI, iJ];\napplySite[psi_, s_, m_, L_] := Flatten[Transpose[m . Transpose[ArrayReshape[psi, {nn^(s - 1), nn, nn^(L - s)}], {2, 1, 3}], {2, 1, 3}]];\ntypesOf[LL_] := Flatten[Table[{\"A\", \"F\"}, LL/2]];\ntransferV[lax_, LL_, ths_, v_, psi_, dA_] := Module[{tys = typesOf[LL], Phi, mat},\n   mat[s_, i_, j_] := N[Normal[lax[tys[[s]]][v, ths[[s]]][i, j]]];\n   Phi = Table[applySite[psi, LL, mat[LL, k, j], LL], {k, dA}, {j, dA}];\n   Do[Phi = Table[Sum[applySite[Phi[[m, j]], s, mat[s, k, m], LL], {m, dA}], {k, dA}, {j, dA}], {s, LL - 1, 1, -1}];\n   Sum[Phi[[i, i]], {i, dA}]];\nthAB[LL_] := N[Flatten[Table[{thA, thF}, LL/2]]];\nt1b[LL_][v_, psi_] := transferV[lax1, LL, thAB[LL], v, psi, 4];\nt2b[LL_][v_, psi_] := transferV[lax2, LL, thAB[LL], v, psi, 6];\nt3b[LL_][v_, psi_] := transferV[lax3, LL, thAB[LL], v, psi, 4];\ndataFile = \"c:\\\\Users\\\\pryan\\\\git-projects\\\\abjm-c123\\\\Paul\\\\Mathematica\\\\su4-alternating\\\\data\\\\abjm-hw-states.wxf\";\nstates = Import[dataFile, \"WXF\"];\nGrid[{{\"loaded\", dataFile}, {\"# states L = 2, 3, 4\", Length /@ {states[\"L2\"], states[\"L3\"], states[\"L4\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"825950\" data-output-id=\"51\" data-out-n=\"535\" data-sub-idx=\"23\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"1\" data-sub-start=\"27\" data-sub-end=\"27\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[535]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.44em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">loaded</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\"># states L = 2, 3, 4</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">c:</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Users</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">pryan</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">git-projects</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">abjm-c123</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Paul</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Mathematica</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">su4-alternating</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">data</span><span class=\"mspace newline\"></span><span class=\"mord\">abjm-hw-states.wxf</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">6</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">26</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">152</span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">}</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[535]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{loaded} & \\text{c:\\\\Users\\\\pryan\\\\git-projects\\\\abjm-c123\\\\Paul\\\\Mathematica\\\\su4-alternating\\\\data\\\\abjm-hw-states.wxf}\\\\\\hline\\text{\\# states L = 2, 3, 4} & \\left\\{6,26,152\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
