  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Eigenvalue polynomials and the Baxter equation\n\nτ̄_a(u) (a = 1, 2, 3, degree 2L) by interpolation at 2L+1 Chebyshev points on [−3, 3]. Baxter operator in polynomial gauge with a trial d(u) ∈ {V₁, V₂, V₄}; the polynomial solution space up to degree D from the coefficient equations (SVD, relative tolerance 10⁻⁹). The right gauge must give, for the vacuum, solutions of degrees 0, 1, 2, 3 (K₁ = K₂ = K₃ = 0).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* nodes shifted off u = 0 (0.^0 is Indeterminate) *)\ntauPolys[LL_, sts_] := Module[{pts = N[3 Cos[Pi (Range[0, LL] + 1/2)/(LL + 1)]] + 0.1234, vand},\n   vand = Table[pt^k, {pt, pts}, {k, 0, LL}];\n   Table[Module[{psi = Normal[st[\"psi\"]], p}, p = Ordering[Abs[psi], -1][[1]];\n     Table[LinearSolve[vand, Table[op[pt, psi][[p]]/psi[[p]], {pt, pts}]], {op, {t1b[LL], t2b[LL], t3b[LL]}}]], {st, sts}]];\npolyOf[c_][x_] := c . x^Range[0, Length[c] - 1];\n(* full tau_a as functions of x for one state, L pairs *)\ntauFull[tc_, L_] := {1 &, polyOf[tc[[1]]], gProd2[L][#] polyOf[tc[[2]]][#] &, gProd3[L][#] polyOf[tc[[3]]][#] &, tau4[L]};\nbaxterMat[tc_, L_, dfun_, D_] := Module[{tf = tauFull[tc, L], cs = Array[cc, D + 1, 0], Q, B},\n   Q[y_] := cs . y^Range[0, D];\n   B = Expand[Sum[(-1)^a tf[[a + 1]][x] Q[x + hh - a hh] Product[dfun[x - b hh], {b, a, 3}], {a, 0, 4}]];\n   Normal[CoefficientArrays[CoefficientList[B, x], cs][[2]]]];\nsolDims[tc_, L_, dfun_, Dmax_] := Table[Module[{M = N[baxterMat[tc, L, dfun, D]], sv}, sv = SingularValueList[M, Tolerance -> 0]; Count[sv/Max[sv], s_ /; s < 10^-9] + (D + 1 - Length[sv])], {D, 0, Dmax}];\ntc2 = tauPolys[4, states[\"L2\"]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{\"d = V\" <> ToString[k], solDims[tc2[[1]], 2, Vv[k][2], 7]}, {k, {1, 2, 4}}], {\"gauge\", \"vacuum (L = 2): dim of polynomial solutions of degree ≤ D, D = 0..7\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
