   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**L = 2:** deg Q₁, Q₁₂, Q₁₂₃ = K₁, K₂, K₃ for every state, Casoratian remainders 10⁻¹³. LR-symmetric states have Q₁(u) = Q₁₂₃(u + h) exactly (10⁻¹⁶); the free shift fitted for the adjoint pair is complex (½ ∓ 0.289i), i.e. not the LR shift. So the LR condition in Q-language is **Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(u + h)** with the fixed shift h (from 𝒫: t̄₃(u+h) ↔ t̄₁(u)). Test it on all states with c = h fixed, against the transfer-matrix defect δ_LR, and check that 𝒫 maps Q₁ of Ψ to Q₁₂₃ of its partner.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**L = 2, 3:** the τ criterion δ_LR = 0 and the Q criterion Q₁(u) = Q₁₂₃(u+h) select exactly the same states (4 of 6, 8 of 26), and **every** state has a partner (𝒫Ψ) with Q₁(partner) = Q₁₂₃(u+h) — LR-symmetric states are their own partner.\n\n### Speed-up for L = 4\n\nEvery Lax entry is diagonal plus at most one e_kl, so the site action only needs scaled slice additions (no 4×4 contraction, no transposes). Same results, checked against the old applySite.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[applySite];\napplySite[psi_, s_, m_, L_] := Module[{A = ArrayReshape[psi, {nn^(s - 1), nn, nn^(L - s)}], R, nz},\n   nz = Select[Flatten[Table[{i, j, m[[i, j]]}, {i, nn}, {j, nn}], 1], #[[3]] != 0 &];\n   R = 0. A;\n   Do[R[[All, r[[1]], All]] += r[[3]] A[[All, r[[2]], All]], {r, nz}];\n   Flatten[R]];\n(* validate against the L = 3 polynomials computed with the old (dense) site action, and time one L = 4 pass *)\nModule[{new, t, psi = Developer`ToPackedArray[N[Normal[states[\"L4\"][[5]][\"psi\"]]] + 0. I]},\n  {t, new} = AbsoluteTiming[tauPolys[6, states[\"L3\"][[{3, 10, 20}]]]];\n  Grid[{{\"max |τ̄ coefficients new − old| (3 states, L = 3)\", Max[Abs[Flatten[new - tc3[[{3, 10, 20}]]]]]},\n    {\"t̄₁ pass at L = 4 (s)\", First[AbsoluteTiming[t1b[8][0.37, psi]]]}, {\"t̄₂ pass at L = 4 (s)\", First[AbsoluteTiming[t2b[8][0.37, psi]]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"825950\" data-output-id=\"60\" data-out-n=\"612\" data-sub-idx=\"3\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"12\" data-sub-start=\"7\" data-sub-end=\"10\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[612]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"wolfbook-render-error\" style=\"color:#cc0000;font-family:monospace;white-space:pre-wrap\">[LaTeX error] KaTeX parse error: Expected &#39;$&#39;, got &#39;$̄&#39; at position 43: …text{max |$\\tau$̲̲̄ coefficients n…<br><small>\\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{max |$\\tau$̄ coefficients new − old| (3 states, L = 3)} &amp; 1.6413537196058314\\times 10^{-12}\\\\\\hline\\text{t̄₁ pass at L = 4 (s)} &amp; 1.6135478\\\\\\hline\\text{t̄₂ pass at L = 4 (s)} &amp; 5.1760976\\\\\\hline\\end{array}</small></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[612]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|}\\hline\\text{max |$\\tau$̄ coefficients new − old| (3 states, L = 3)} & 1.6413537196058314\\times 10^{-12}\\\\\\hline\\text{t̄₁ pass at L = 4 (s)} & 1.6135478\\\\\\hline\\text{t̄₂ pass at L = 4 (s)} & 5.1760976\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
