  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### L = 4: Q-functions, LR summary for L = 2, 3, 4, and saving all Q's to `data/abjm-Qfunctions.wxf`",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "vacQ[4] = solveQs[tc4[[1]], 4, 22];\nqRows[4] = MapThread[qRow[#1, #2, 4, vacQ[4]] &, {states[\"L4\"], tc4}];\nqCheck = Table[{L, Length[qRows[L]], Count[qRows[L], r_ /; r[\"degQ\"] == r[\"K\"]], Max[#rem & /@ qRows[L]]}, {L, {2, 3, 4}}];\nlrRows = Table[With[{s = lrSummary[L]}, {L, Length[s], Count[s[[All, 2]], True], Count[s[[All, 3]], True], Count[s, {_, a_, a_, _}], Count[s[[All, 4]], True]}], {L, {2, 3, 4}}];\nqFile = FileNameJoin[{DirectoryName[dataFile], \"abjm-Qfunctions.wxf\"}];\nExport[qFile, <|\"description\" -> \"Q-functions (monic polynomials in x = u) of the states in abjm-hw-states.wxf (same order): Q1, Q12, Q123 from the Baxter equation sum_a (-1)^a tau_a(u) Q(u+h-ah) prod_{b=a}^{3} V4(u-bh) = 0 (V4 = vacuum T_44 eigenvalue), Q12, Q123 = Casoratians divided by the vacuum ones. K = magnon numbers, degQ = degrees, roots, LR flags: dLR (transfer-matrix defect), Q1 vs Q123(u+h). abjm-Qfunctions.wb, 2026-10-12.\",\n    \"L2\" -> qRows[2], \"L3\" -> qRows[3], \"L4\" -> qRows[4]|>, \"WXF\"];\nGrid[Join[{{\"L\", \"# states\", \"# with deg(Q₁, Q₁₂, Q₁₂₃) = (K₁, K₂, K₃)\", \"max Casoratian remainder\"}}, qCheck,\n   {{\"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"L\", \"# states\", \"# LR by τ\", \"# LR by Q\", \"# τ and Q agree\", \"# with LR partner\"}}, lrRows, {{\"saved\", qFile, \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
