  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12)\n\n- **Q-functions for all 184 states** (L = 2, 3, 4 pairs) from the 4th-order Baxter equation in the gauge d = V₄ (fixed by the vacuum: Σ(−1)^aτ_a D^a = (1−V₁D)(1−V₂D)(1−V₃D)(1−V₄D)); Q₁₂, Q₁₂₃ = Casoratians / vacuum Casoratians. Every state: deg(Q₁, Q₁₂, Q₁₂₃) = (K₁, K₂, K₃), remainders ≤ 8·10⁻¹². Saved in `data/abjm-Qfunctions.wxf` (with τ̄ polynomials for L = 4 in `data/abjm-tau-L4.wxf`).\n- **LR symmetry in Q-language: Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(u + h).** It holds exactly for precisely the states with τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₃(u+h): 4/6, 8/26, 24/152. Every other state has an LR partner (𝒫Ψ) with Q₁(partner) = Q₁₂₃(u+h) (all 184 states). So the ABJM spectrum is LR-symmetric (Q₁ ↔ Q₁₂₃ with shift h, i.e. Q_j ↔ Q^{5−j}), states being LR singlets or LR doublets — the same structure as in 2603. What fails is only the selection rule for the note's 3-pt configuration (`abjm-LR-symmetry.wb`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "lrFixed[q1_, q123_] := Module[{r1 = rootsOf[q1], r3 = rootsOf[q123]},\n   Which[Length[r1] != Length[r3], Infinity, Length[r1] == 0, 0., True, Max[Table[Min[Abs[r1 - (s - hh)]], {s, r3}]]]];\n(* LR partner = the state whose tau1 equals my tau3(u+h): match by Q1(partner) = Q123(me)(u+h) *)\npartnerRes[row_, rows_] := Min[Table[If[r[\"degQ\"][[1]] == row[\"degQ\"][[3]] && r[\"dyn\"] == Reverse[row[\"dyn\"]], lrFixed[r[\"Q1\"], row[\"Q123\"]], Infinity], {r, rows}]];\nlrSummary[L_] := Module[{rows = qRows[L]},\n   Table[{r[\"dyn\"], r[\"dLR\"] < 10^-8, lrFixed[r[\"Q1\"], r[\"Q123\"]] < 10^-6, partnerRes[r, rows] < 10^-6}, {r, rows}]];\nGrid[{{\"L\", \"# states\", \"# LR by τ (δ_LR < 10⁻⁸)\", \"# LR by Q (Q₁ = Q₁₂₃(u+h))\", \"# where τ and Q criteria agree\", \"# with a partner: Q₁(partner) = Q₁₂₃(u+h)\"},\n  Sequence @@ Table[With[{s = lrSummary[L]}, {L, Length[s], Count[s[[All, 2]], True], Count[s[[All, 3]], True], Count[s, {_, a_, a_, _}], Count[s[[All, 4]], True]}], {L, {2, 3}}]}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"825950\" data-output-id=\"59\" data-out-n=\"605\" data-sub-idx=\"4\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"11\" data-sub-start=\"6\" data-sub-end=\"7\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[605]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:3.64em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.09em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:3.6em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-1.55em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:2.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-4.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">L</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-1.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.55em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arr